Home range estimation
We delineate individual home ranges by computing minimum convex polygons (MCP) via convex hulls (chull) using projected UTM coordinates. We retain individuals with at least 4 spatially-reference captures and filter out coordinate points \(&gt; 150\text{ m}\) from each individual’s mean centroid to remove GPS artifacts and/or potential misidentifications. The resulting polygon coordinates are saved to data/home_ranges.rds and visualized with site-mean-centered coordinates to compare spatial extents across elevation sites.

home_ranges &lt;- mr_data |&gt;
  filter(if_all(c(lat, lon, utm_x, utm_y), ~ !is.na(.x))) |&gt;
  group_by(site, id, sex) |&gt;
  mutate(
    n_obs = n(),
    mean_utm_x = mean(utm_x),
    mean_utm_y = mean(utm_y),
    dist_to_center = sqrt((utm_x - mean_utm_x)^2 + (utm_y - mean_utm_y)^2)
  ) |&gt;
  filter(
    dist_to_center &lt;= 150,
    n_obs &gt;= 4
  ) |&gt;
  slice(chull(utm_x, utm_y)) |&gt;
  ungroup() |&gt;
  select(site, id, sex, utm_x, utm_y)

saveRDS(home_ranges, file = "data/home_ranges.rds")



